@ 5:6  the|me: dark
  5:3-5:8 "theme"
  | **theme**
  |
  | Theme, the CSS style sheet.
  | You may also use `themeCSS` to override this value.
  |
  | Type: `"default" | "base" | "dark" | "forest" | "neutral" | "neo" | "neo-dark" | "redux" | "redux-dark" | "redux-color" | "redux-dark-color" | "auto" | "null"` · Default: `"redux-color"`
  |
  | Status: honoured (since 13.0.0). The default changes from `default` to `redux-color`, the theme v12's flowchart renders by default (D151, amending D55). 13.0 ships the redux family (`redux`, `redux-color`, `redux-dark`, `redux-dark-color`) as real themes, plus `default`, `dark`, `forest`, `neutral` and `base`. `neo` renders `redux-color`, `neo-dark` renders `redux-dark-color` and `null` renders `base`, each with a `THEME_UNAVAILABLE` warning.
