@ 9:8  cur|ve: basis
  9:5-9:10 "curve"
  | **flowchart.curve**
  |
  | Defines how mermaid renders curves for flowcharts.
  |
  | Type: `"basis" | "bumpX" | "bumpY" | "cardinal" | "catmullRom" | "linear" | "monotoneX" | "monotoneY" | "natural" | "step" | "stepAfter" | "stepBefore" | "rounded"` · Default: `"rounded"`
  |
  | Status: honoured (since 13.0.0). The default changes from `basis` to `rounded`, the look of v12's default ELK layout: stepped routes whose corners are arcs of radius 5 (less on a short leg). Set `basis` to keep S-curves. `linear` draws straight segments; `step`, `stepBefore` and `stepAfter` draw stepped routes; `rounded` draws straight segments with rounded corners; every other value draws S-curves (the layout engine routes edges, not a d3 curve factory).
@ 10:13  htmlLabe|ls: true
  10:5-10:15 "htmlLabels"
  | **flowchart.htmlLabels**
  |
  | **DEPRECATED: Use global `htmlLabels` instead.**
  |
  | Flag for setting whether or not a html tag should be used for rendering labels on nodes and edges.
  | This property is deprecated.
  | Please use the global `htmlLabels` configuration instead.
  |
  | Type: `boolean | null` · Default: `null`
  |
  | Status: removed (since 13.0.0). Labels are SVG text only; there is no HTML label mode (D5). Replacement: none; labels support a markdown subset rendered as SVG text.
